definitions.content:
“Account Bank Event” means, in respect of an Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank, any of:
the occurrence of an Insolvency Event;
it being or becoming subject to Insolvency Proceedings;
to the extent such Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank is an Electronic Money Institution, an “insolvency event” occurs with respect to it or it becomes subject to “insolvency proceedings”, each as defined in the Electronic Money Regulations 2011/99;
to the extent that such Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank is an Electronic Money Institution as at the date on which it is appointed to act as an Account Bank for the purposes of this Transaction, on any subsequent date it is no longer registered or authorised as an Electronic Money Institution;
the occurrence of an Account Bank Downgrade; or
any event of default (or equivalent event) or breach by the Issuer Account Bank or Collections Account Bank, as the case may be, is continuing in respect of the relevant account bank under the Issuer Account Bank Agreement or any Acknowledgment of Collections Account Declaration of Trust executed by the account bank.
